celebrate together."

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:57.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
You still must feel optimistic
about the season.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do, yeah.
I mean, we're 11-1.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.462 line:92%
You know, our loss yesterday

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:06.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
dropped us to the number-one
seed in the AFC.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're still okay.
-We're still okay.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:12.305 size:81% position:41%
I'm very much enjoying
this bald hairstyle.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.875
A couple weeks ago, you were
rocking this, which is, uh..

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, again,
this was for a role.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I believe what you have no
is for a role, right?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.715 size:78% position:39%
These are not choices
that you're making

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.018 size:81% position:41% line:92%
based on how it looks.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well...
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:30.557
-I could hear, like, a littl
tinge of something in your voice

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.125 size:88% position:44% line:92%
as you said that, but...

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I had a white Mohawk
for a job,

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I have bald head
for a job.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:41.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
In between, I got to, yes,
make some life choices,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.003 line:92%
and the blue Mohawk was for me

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:47.240 size:84% position:42%
-I'm very excited about
your white Mohawk job,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm curious if your wife
Sofia Vergara --

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
is she happy when you have
white Mohawk jobs?

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.652 line:92%
-I think she's happy with --

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
happiest with jobs

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
in which I look like I looke
when we first met.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:08.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, there's something
about that.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like putting water
in the cement mix --

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.198 line:92%
it just creates concrete.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:15.268
Like, whenever you meet, that'
the way she wants me to stay

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.437
But, you know, she knew
she was marrying an actor

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:21.474
and she knew it was gonna ge
weird at some point, Seth,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it has.
-With that said,

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:23.710 line:92%
you married an actor, too,

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she's looked the exact sam
for like 20 years.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.314 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's correct.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.318 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I am not looking forward

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.321 line:92%
to her white Mohawk role.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.523 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Very fair.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.323 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This is a cool part.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play a character
named Max Fist.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.294 line:92%
Tell us a little bit about it.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, Max Fist is,
for me --

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, the character
I'm playing --

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:49.969 line:92%
he's a meth-addicted alcoholic

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.840 line:92%
homeless, maybe schizophrenic,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.409 line:92%
has some psychotic episodes,

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.913
you know, bum who lives
in a tent under a bridge.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was a whole different,
you know, movie for me.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't really play
the superhero.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.690
The thing is, is he has thes
delusions or these visions

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.060
or dreams or maybe they're
memories -- he's not sure --

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he was, like,
the champion,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.265 size:84% position:42%
a superpower champion
from another dimension,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.868
and that's really what he
believes, who he believes he is.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.837
And you just don't know if he is
or if he isn't.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:29.475
-It's very cool, and I kno
you're someone who, like myself,

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
growing up, I think we liked
the idea of heroes,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.713 size:78% position:39% line:92%
we liked comic books,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.982
and obviously, you've had
experience doing that.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:38.284 size:75% position:38%
In 2002, you were in
that "Spider-Man,"

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:41.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I did not realize
that you actually auditioned

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to play Spider-Man,

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
the role that Tobey Maguir
ended up playing.

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:50.663 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, all the young men
who appear in the film,

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
we all auditioned
to play Peter Parker.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:56.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tobey obviously auditioned
to play Peter Parker,

00:03:56.236 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
James Franco screen-tested
as Peter Parker,

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:06.079
and I originally auditione
for Peter Parker when I went in.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:11.150
We all read the same sides and
then were nudged into our roles.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you know
that you weren't, maybe,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a perfect fit
for Peter Parker?

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because this would be a case
where he would be, like,

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.725 line:92%
bitten by a radioactive spider

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.094 size:75% position:38%
that made him, like,
a little bit weaker?

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:21.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Sure.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:26.899
I mean, you know, the trope or
the archetype of Peter Parke

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.102 line:92%
is that he's this, like, nerd.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:33.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's, you know, very smart
but not the cool guy at school

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:40.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he is in love with
the cool guy's girlfriend.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:44.484 line:92%
And so, I knew that, you know,

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter how much of a nerd
I am on the inside,

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm never going to get cas
as Peter Parker,

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
I'm 6'5", 200-whatever.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:56.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
So finding the bullies for m
would be really odd.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:57.797 line:92%
I just didn't fit that role.

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:03.670
I knew that I'd fit the part
of Flash, or the bully, better

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:08.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I actually came prepared
I learned those scenes

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:11.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
and was off-book on them
when I got there.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when I read to play
Peter Parker,

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had glasses on
and a button-down shirt.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the casting director said,
"You know, that was great,

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you're never gonna get
this role."

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:19.886 line:92%
I said, "I know, I know."

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said, "But there's thi
other part."

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Flash."
She said, "Yeah."

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said, "That's probably
better for you."

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.693 line:92%
I go, "Oh, great." I go...

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:27.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she goes, "Let me go
get the script."

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "No, no, no, I've got it
I'm off-book, let's go."

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.164 line:92%
And I took off the glasses

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.032 size:84% position:42%
and started unbuttoning
the button-down shirt

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.400 line:92%
and I had a tank top underneat

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I went straight into
the Flash sides.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at the end, she said,
"I want you to meet Sam Raimi.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:43.609 size:75% position:38%
And she got me a job
the following week

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:51.184
that paid me $500 to screen-test
as Flash on film

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
against the other
Spider-Man candidates.

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.255 line:92%
One of them was James Franco

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.023 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Ah, that is incredible.

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:59.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think a good lesson
to all actors

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:02.962
to be a little bit more prepared
than they even ask you to.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.297 size:81% position:41% line:92%
A nice ending for you.

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:06.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's always great
to see you.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for making time
for us today, Joe.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:10.002 line:92%
-Thanks, man. Go Steelers.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Go Steelers.
"Archenemy" is in theaters

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
on demand and digital
December 11th.

